{"title":"Math textbooks","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>This <b>Math textbooks</b> page is for compiling a list of <b>textbooks</b> for mathematics -- not problem books, contest books, or general interest books.  See <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math books\">math books</a> for more titles.\n</p><p>Before adding any books to this page, please review the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki:Linking_books\" title=\"AoPS Wiki:Linking books\">AoPS Wiki:Linking books</a> page.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Math_textbooks_by_subject\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Math textbooks by subject</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Algebra\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Algebra</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Getting_Started\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Getting Started</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Calculus\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Calculus</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#High_School/College_1st_year\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">High School/College 1st year</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Collegiate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Collegiate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Combinatorics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Combinatorics</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Getting_Started_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Getting Started</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Intermediate_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Collegiate_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Collegiate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Geometry\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geometry</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Getting_Started_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Getting Started</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Intermediate_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Collegiate_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Collegiate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Number_Theory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Number Theory</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Getting_Started_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Getting Started</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Collegiate_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Collegiate</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-4 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Analytic_Number_Theory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5.2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Analytic Number Theory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-4 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Elliptic_Curves\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5.2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Elliptic Curves</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Probability_and_Statistics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Probability and Statistics</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Getting_Started_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Getting Started</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Intermediate_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-24\"><a href=\"#Collegiate_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Collegiate</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-25\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Math_textbooks_by_subject\">Math textbooks by subject</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Math textbooks by subject\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Levels of reading and math ability are loosely defined as follows:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Elementary is for elementary school students up through possibly early middle school.</li>\n<li>Getting Started is recommended for students grades 6 to 9.</li>\n<li>Intermediate is recommended for students grades 9 to 12.</li>\n<li>Collegiate is recommended for college and university students.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Algebra\">Algebra</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Algebra\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Getting_Started\">Getting Started</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Getting Started\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes Dr. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Richard_Rusczyk\" title=\"Richard Rusczyk\">Richard Rusczyk</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/store/book/intro-algebra\">Introduction to Algebra</a> textbook, which is recommended for advanced middle and high school students.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0669431605/artofproblems-20\">Algebra I: An Integrated Approach</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0079039898/artofproblems-20\">Algebra 1</a> published by McGrawHill.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes Dr. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Richard_Rusczyk\" title=\"Richard Rusczyk\">Richard Rusczyk</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/store/book/intermediate-algebra\">Intermediate Algebra</a> textbook, which is recommended for advanced middle and high school students.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.pearson.com/en-us/subject-catalog/p/algebra-and-trigonometry/P200000011699/9780138251406\">Algebra and Trigonometry</a> by Michael Sullivan.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/039567610X/artofproblems-20\">Algebra and Trigonometry: Structure and Method, Book 2</a> by Brown, Dolciani, Sorgenfrey, and Kane.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0079039901/artofproblems-20\">Algebra 2</a> published by McGrawHill.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Calculus\">Calculus</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Calculus\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span id=\"High_School.2FCollege_1st_year\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"High_School/College_1st_year\">High School/College 1st year</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: High School/College 1st year\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0521867444/artofproblems-20\">Calculus</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Michael_Spivak&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Michael Spivak (page does not exist)\">Michael Spivak</a>.  Top students swear by this book.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0357749146/artofproblems-20\">Calculus Of A Single Variable</a> by Ron Larson and Bruce Edwards.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/store/book/calculus\">Calculus</a> by Dr. David Patrick, which is recommended for advanced high school students.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1337624187/artofproblems-20\">Calculus</a> by James Stewart. This is the most commonly used calculus textbook for the AP tests.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1119696550/artofproblems-20\">Calculus: Single and Multivariable</a> by Deborah Hughes-Hallett, Andrew M. Gleason, and William G. McCallum.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Collegiate\">Collegiate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Collegiate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0805390219/artofproblems-20\">Calculus on Manifolds: A Modern Approach to Classical Theorems of Advanced Calculus</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Michael_Spivak&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Michael Spivak (page does not exist)\">Michael Spivak</a>.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Combinatorics\">Combinatorics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Combinatorics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Getting_Started_2\">Getting Started</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Getting Started\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes Dr. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=David_Patrick\" title=\"David Patrick\">David Patrick</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/store/item/intro-counting\">Introduction to Counting &amp; Probability</a> textbook, which is recommended for advanced middle and high school students.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate_2\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes Dr. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=David_Patrick\" title=\"David Patrick\">David Patrick</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/store/book/intermediate-counting\">Intermediate Counting &amp; Probability</a> textbook, which is recommended for advanced middle and high school students.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Collegiate_2\">Collegiate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Collegiate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-0-8176-8154-8\">A Path to Combinatorics for Undergraduates</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Titu_Andreescu\" title=\"Titu Andreescu\">Titu Andreescu</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Zuming_Feng&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Zuming Feng (page does not exist)\">Zuming Feng</a>.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geometry\">Geometry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Geometry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Getting_Started_3\">Getting Started</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Getting Started\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Richard_Rusczyk\" title=\"Richard Rusczyk\">Richard Rusczyk</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//artofproblemsolving.com/store/book/intro-geometry\">Introduction to Geometry</a> textbook, which is recommended for advanced middle and high school students.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-2022-8\">Geometry</a> by Serge Lang and Gene Murrow.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0395977274/artofproblems-20\">Geometry</a> by Ray C. Jurgensen.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0076639290/artofproblems-20\">Geometry</a> published by McGrawHill.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate_3\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.wiley.com/en-us/Advanced+Euclidean+Geometry%3A+Excursions+for+Secondary+Teachers+and+Students-p-9780470412565\">Advanced Euclidean Geometry</a> by Alfred S. Posamentier.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=NML/19\">Geometry Revisited</a> -- Not a traditional textbook, but close enough to list this classic.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//bookstore.ams.org/view?ProductCode=CLRM/37\">Methods for Euclidean Geometry</a> by Owen Byer, Felix Lazebnik, and Deirdre L. Smeltzer.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Collegiate_3\">Collegiate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Collegiate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//store.doverpublications.com/collections/math-geometry/products/9780486658124\">Geometry: A Comprehensive Course</a> by Dan Pedoe.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Number_Theory\">Number Theory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Number Theory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Getting_Started_4\">Getting Started</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Getting Started\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Books/AoPS_B_Item.php?page_id=10\">Introduction to Number Theory</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathew_Crawford\" title=\"Mathew Crawford\">Mathew Crawford</a>.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Collegiate_4\">Collegiate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Collegiate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.mheducation.com/highered/product/elementary-number-theory-burton.html?viewOption=student\">Elementary Number Theory</a> by David M. Burton</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-0-387-54109-9\">Quadratic Diophantine Equations</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Titu_Andreescu\" title=\"Titu Andreescu\">Titu Andreescu</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dorin_Andrica&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Dorin Andrica (page does not exist)\">Dorin Andrica</a>.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-030-98931-6\">Explorations in Number Theory</a> by Cam McLeman, Erin McNicholas, and Colin Starr.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-981-16-9150-8\">A Textbook of Algebraic Number Theory</a> by Sudesh Kaur Khanduja.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-030-73169-4\">Excursions in Multiplicative Number Theory</a> by Olivier Ramare.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//global.oup.com/academic/product/an-introduction-to-the-theory-of-numbers-9780199219865?cc=us&amp;lang=en&amp;\">An Introduction to the Theory of Numbers</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=G._H._Hardy\" title=\"G. H. Hardy\">G. H. Hardy</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edward_M._Wright&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Edward M. Wright (page does not exist)\">Edward M. Wright</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Andrew_Wiles\" title=\"Andrew Wiles\">Andrew Wiles</a> (6th Edition).</li></ul>\n<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Analytic_Number_Theory\">Analytic Number Theory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Analytic Number Theory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h5>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-5579-4\">Introduction to Analytic Number Theory</a> by Tom M. Apostol.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.cambridge.org/us/universitypress/subjects/mathematics/number-theory/primer-analytic-number-theory-pythagoras-riemann?format=PB\">A Primer of Analytic Number Theory</a> by Jeffrey Stopple.</li></ul>\n<h5><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Elliptic_Curves\">Elliptic Curves</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Elliptic Curves\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h5>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.cambridge.org/us/universitypress/subjects/mathematics/geometry-and-topology/elliptic-curves-function-theory-geometry-arithmetic?format=PB\">Elliptic Curves: Function Theory, Geometry, Arithmetic</a> by Henry McKean and Victor Moll.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Probability_and_Statistics\">Probability and Statistics</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Probability and Statistics\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Getting_Started_5\">Getting Started</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Getting Started\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes Dr. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=David_Patrick\" title=\"David Patrick\">David Patrick</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Books/AoPS_B_Item.php?page_id=3\">Introduction to Counting &amp; Probability</a> textbook, which is recommended for advanced middle and high school students.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate_4\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AoPS\">AoPS</a> publishes Dr. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=David_Patrick\" title=\"David Patrick\">David Patrick</a>'s <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/store/item/intermediate-counting\">Intermediate Counting &amp; Probability</a> textbook, which is recommended for advanced middle and high school students.</li></ul>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Collegiate_5\">Collegiate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24\" title=\"Edit section: Collegiate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0824703790/artofproblems-20\">Probability and Statistical Inference</a> by Nitis Mukhopadhyay.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4286-2\">Statistical Decision Theory and Bayesian Analysis</a> by James O. Berger.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.routledge.com/Bayesian-Data-Analysis/Gelman-Carlin-Stern-Dunson-Vehtari-Rubin/p/book/9781439840955\">Bayesian Data Analysis</a> by Andrew Gelman, John B. Carlin, Hal S. Stern, David B. Dunson, Aki Vehtari, and Donald B. Rubin.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.routledge.com/Markov-Chain-Monte-Carlo-in-Practice/Gilks-Richardson-Spiegelhalter/p/book/9780412055515\">Markov Chain Monte Carlo in Practice</a> by W.R. Gilks.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4145-2\">Monte Carlo Statistical Methods</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_textbooks&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_books\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math books\">Math books</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Science_books\" title=\"Science books\">Science books</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174949\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.034 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 103/1000000\nPo